that every citizen has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of Violence;
that Women and Children are among vulnerable groups who tend to experience Violence which constitutes an act that violates human rights and need to receive legal Protection;
that the implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence needs to be supported by institutions and regulations so as to guarantee its implementation;
that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence;

